However, we can infer some general approaches that are applicable across Azure services based on the patterns observed in the documentation:

1. **Enable Diagnostic Settings**: For most Azure resources, including App Service, you can enable diagnostic settings to send logs and metrics to a Log Analytics workspace.
   ```json
   {
     "name": "appServiceDiagnosticSettings",
     "type": "Microsoft.Web/sites/config",
     "properties": {
       "logs": [
         {
           "category": "All",
           "enabled": true,
           "retentionPolicy": {
             "days": 30,
             "enabled": true
           }
         }
       ],
       "metrics": [
         {
           "category": "AllMetrics",
           "enabled": true
         }
       ],
       "workspaceResourceId": "/subscriptions/{subscription-id}/resourceGroups/{resource-group-name}/providers/Microsoft.OperationalInsights/workspaces/{workspace-name}"
     }
   }
   ```
   [Source: azure/AKS/Monitor Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) > AKS monitoring data: metrics, logs, integrations]

2. **Configure Alerts in Azure Monitor**: Use Azure Monitor to create alerts based on metrics or log queries.
   - **Metric Alerts**: Evaluate resource metrics at regular intervals.
     ```json
     {
       "name": "appServiceMetricAlert",
       "type": "Microsoft.Insights/metricAlerts",
       "properties": {
         "description": "High CPU usage alert for App Service",
         "severity": 3,
         "scopes": [
           "/subscriptions/{subscription-id}/resourceGroups/{resource-group-name}/providers/Microsoft.Web/sites/{app-service-name}"
         ],
         "condition": {
           "metricName": "Percentage CPU",
           "namespace": "",
           "operator": "GreaterThan",
           "threshold": 80,
           "timeGrain": "PT1M",
           "aggregation": "Average",
           "windowSize": "PT5M"
         },
         "actions": [
           {
             "name": "EmailOpsTeam",
             "targetResourceId": "/subscriptions/{subscription-id}/resourceGroups/{resource-group-name}/providers/Microsoft.Resources/webhooks/{webhook-name}"
           }
         ]
       }
     }
     ```
   - **Log Alerts**: Use Log Analytics queries to evaluate resource logs.
     ```json
     {
       "name": "appServiceLogAlert",
       "type": "Microsoft.Insights/alertRules",
       "properties": {
         "description": "Alert on failed requests in App Service",
         "severity": 2,
         "enabled": true,
         "targetResourceId": "/subscriptions/{subscription-id}/resourceGroups/{resource-group-name}/providers/Microsoft.Web/sites/{app-service-name}",
         "condition": {
           "odata.type": "Microsoft.Azure.Management.Insights.Models.RuleCondition",
           "metricName": "FailedRequests",
           "operator": "GreaterThanValue",
           "threshold": 10,
           "timeAggregation": "Total"
         },
         "actionProfileId": "/subscriptions/{subscription-id}/resourceGroups/{resource-group-name}/providers/Microsoft.AlertsManagement/actionProfiles/emailOpsTeam"
       }
     }
     ```
   [Source: azure/Virtual Machines > Monitor Azure Virtual Machines > Alerts > Types of alerts]

3. **Use Application Insights**: For App Service, integrating with Application Insights provides detailed performance and usage analytics.
   ```json
   {
     "name": "appServiceAppInsights",
     "type": "Microsoft.Web/sites/config",
     "properties": {
       "siteName": "{app-service-name}",
       "applicationInsights": {
         "id": "/subscriptions/{subscription-id}/resourceGroups/{resource-group-name}/providers/Microsoft.Insights/components/{ai-component-name}"
       }
     }
   }
   ```
   [Source: azure/Azure Functions > Migrate AWS Lambda workloads to Azure Functions > Optimize and monitor the application's performance on Azure]

